": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bfccf572105dd080c3718a305a96018919b3876b250f515e90988ca50ef11c10","event_uuid":"e863aeb5-a168-4122-bf53-c6e0bc7ae6c0","position":{"commit_sha":"5412657e458d5357c5b440855ad784afbb55c0cd","position":"1786741193337824001-e863aeb5-a168-4122-bf53-c6e0bc7ae6c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"16d9ed5cc7d24c17c43a4264d74dd3c2d24b767b62024e10eece6f12accfb616","event_uuid":"19087e1f-df91-46eb-9c23-120e3a20a788","position":{"commit_sha":"bee8b198313719c38be084efd5971fd311468743","position":"1786741303007178001-19087e1f-df91-46eb-9c23-120e3a20a788"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786741181909376001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e863aeb5-a168-4122-bf53-c6e0bc7ae6c0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fb8a-7363-e406-4e36"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe layered defenses against the attestation-laundering anti-pattern — tagging a CODE-VERIFIABLE acceptance criterion `[operator-attested]` so the completion verifier accepts a ticket comment instead of repository proof — failed to reject a live instance.\n\n## Reproduction (today, epic fb8a-7363-e406-4e36 close)\n1. Epic close failed: completion verifier hit its step budget (request_limit=24) and reported AC-19 unmet — though its proof is repo-resident (tests/unit/test_scan_scoping.py::test_fsck_default_skips_archived_and_flag_restores et al., merged 39de64871c).\n2. The operator retagged AC-19 `[operator-attested]` (the anti-pattern; a misclassification — the evidence is an exact path/symbol repository fact).\n3. `rebar review-plan fb8a-7363-e406-4e36` → PASS. Expected: the evidence-kind criterion (criteria_routing.json \"FIRE on … a tagged repository fact grounded by exact path/symbol evidence\") fires; also the AC carried NO `provenance:` continuation line, which det_measurement_provenance (plan_review/det_measurement_provenance.py) is supposed to require on every tagged AC.\n4. Close succeeded: the completion verifier accepted the tag at face value — correct per its prompt (completion_verifier.md \"How you classify a criterion: SOLELY from an author tag\"; ADR-0043 makes the tag a trust escape hatch), which is exactly why the REVIEW-side guards must be the rejection point.\n\n## Suspected defects (investigate all)\n- Evidence-kind criterion did not fire on a tagged repo-provable AC at re-review time (routing overlay not applied? criterion advisory instead of blocking? re-review of an in_progress ticket skips it?).\n- det_measurement_provenance did not flag the missing `provenance:` line (same questions; det_floor.py wiring says ADVISORY — if so, advisory is insufficient for this class).\n- Consider a deterministic pre-close guard: a criterion whose text cites an exact repo path/symbol (or whose evidence comment does) but carries the tag is auto-rejected before any LLM runs.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified for why the plan-review evidence-kind guard passed a tagged repository fact (with the failing review run cited).\n- [ ] A mistagged code-verifiable AC (repo path/symbol evidence exists) is REJECTED before close: reproduced RED with a fixture ticket, then GREEN after the fix.\n- [ ] A tagged AC missing its `provenance:` continuation line is rejected (or the advisory is promoted to blocking for close-path reviews), with tests.\n- [ ] Legitimately external ACs (deploy/vote/console evidence with provenance) still pass: guard test.\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2f56-313f-6175-41b1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion-close path accepts [operator-attested] on code-verifiable criteria (laundering guard missed)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["10f70a60-613d-4749-bce7-049ac691ecbe","e863aeb5-a168-4122-bf53-c6e0bc7ae6c0","19087e1f-df91-46eb-9c23-120e3a20a788"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786741303007178002,"uuid":"0108efd1-ad0f-4b74-813a-b5e7e03c6967"}